# Tests that differ from the reference, one a line: the test's name, then
# the reason. tests/rom/run.py reports each as KNOWN, never as ok; a known
# test that starts passing is reported too, so this list is kept true.
#
# Each is a difference contract 2.0 makes on purpose (README.md, Time):
#
# alu: the test reads the multiplier or divider ($4214-$4217) while it
# works, a cycle or a few after its start; the S-CPU's C takes no time, so
# nativeshvc's result is done when read. Every other read and every
# picture matches.
#
# apu: the S-CPU reads the sound unit's port ($2140) as its boot ROM
# replies; the SPC700's work takes no time, so nativeshvc's boot ROM replies
# as soon as it sees the S-CPU's value, before the reference's. Every other
# read and every picture matches.
